IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`
IMPORT `sda-home`

-- Stamp Duty Act 1978 (NT) -- cases for the home-conveyance core (sda-home.l4).
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (reprint REPS013): the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) scale, the
-- s 88(1) amounts and the TAA s 27 rounding, with the arithmetic done in an independent calculator written from the
-- statutory words (scratchpad au-nt-1/calc/hand.py), never copied from this encoding's output. Regulative rules are
-- asserted with EVALTRACE where the trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it ends in a
-- breach or a pending obligation. Clock: days.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Stamp Duty Act 1978; see SOURCE-LICENSE.md.

§ `Cases -- the conveyee of a home`

§§ `A purchase, with the facts most cases share`

-- One or two individual buyers, citizens, of full age, buying the whole of the land for themselves with a home on it,
-- who will all live in it, with possession at settlement. The parameters are the facts that vary between cases.
GIVEN `day`                            IS A DATE
      `price`                          IS A NUMBER
      `a first home buyer`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `had Territory residential property in the last 24 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a new home`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `a senior`                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `a grant`                        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Home conveyance`
`a purchase` MEANS
    `Home conveyance` WITH
        `the date first executed`                                                         IS `day`
        `the consideration`                                                               IS `price`
        `the unencumbered value`                                                          IS `price`
        `there is a home on the land at the relevant time`                                IS TRUE
        `it is an off-the-plan contract`                                                  IS FALSE
        `every conveyee is an individual`                                                 IS TRUE
        `at least one conveyee is 18 or older, or is exempted from the age requirement`   IS TRUE
        `at least one conveyee is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`            IS TRUE
        `at least one conveyee is 60 or older at the relevant time`                       IS `a senior`
        `at least one conveyee holds an NT pensioner, carer or concession scheme card`     IS FALSE
        `a conveyee or spouse has received the first home owner concession before`        IS FALSE
        `a conveyee or spouse has had a relevant interest in a residence they occupied`   IS (NOT `a first home buyer`)
        `a conveyee or spouse has received a grant, discount, concession or rebate before, not repaid` IS FALSE
        `a conveyee or spouse has had a relevant interest in residential property`        IS (NOT `a first home buyer`)
        `a conveyee or spouse had a relevant interest in Territory residential property in the 24 months before` IS `had Territory residential property in the last 24 months`
        `the Commissioner exempts that Territory interest for a relationship breakdown`   IS FALSE
        `a conveyee already has a beneficial interest in the land`                        IS FALSE
        `the conveyees will acquire the whole beneficial interest in the land`            IS TRUE
        `a conveyee will acquire an interest in the land as trustee`                      IS FALSE
        `every conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence`       IS TRUE
        `at least one conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence` IS TRUE
        `a conveyee who is 60 or older or holds a card will occupy the home`              IS `a senior`
        `the Commissioner exempts the conveyees from the occupancy requirement`           IS FALSE
        `the home has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`       IS `a new home`
        `the home is substantially renovated new residential premises not occupied or sold since` IS FALSE
        `the Commissioner declares the home a qualifying home`                            IS FALSE
        `a conveyee has been paid, is entitled to or will become entitled to a first home owner grant` IS `a grant`
        `the conveyee is paid the grant for a transaction that commenced from 1 January 2015 to 6 May 2019` IS FALSE
        `the conveyees become entitled to possession within 12 months after settlement`   IS TRUE

-- A builder who meets every s 90D(2)(b), (d)-(h) condition, and the same with one condition missing.
`a building contractor who meets s 90D` MEANS
    `New home from a building contractor` WITH
        `it replaces a conveyance first executed before 1 July 2022, or rests on an option granted before then` IS FALSE
        `the conveyees agree to acquire title to and the whole beneficial interest in land owned by a building contractor` IS TRUE
        `the building contractor agrees to convey the land to the conveyees`                                IS TRUE
        `the building contractor agrees to build, place, complete or convey a detached, new home on the land` IS TRUE
        `the building contractor owns the land before execution, or will before settlement`               IS TRUE
        `the building contractor bought the land from the person who developed it as a residential lot`  IS TRUE
        `the building contractor paid duty on the land's dutiable value when buying it from the developer` IS TRUE

`a building contractor who bought the land from someone other than the developer` MEANS
    `New home from a building contractor` WITH
        `it replaces a conveyance first executed before 1 July 2022, or rests on an option granted before then` IS FALSE
        `the conveyees agree to acquire title to and the whole beneficial interest in land owned by a building contractor` IS TRUE
        `the building contractor agrees to convey the land to the conveyees`                                IS TRUE
        `the building contractor agrees to build, place, complete or convey a detached, new home on the land` IS TRUE
        `the building contractor owns the land before execution, or will before settlement`               IS TRUE
        `the building contractor bought the land from the person who developed it as a residential lot`  IS FALSE
        `the building contractor paid duty on the land's dutiable value when buying it from the developer` IS TRUE

`a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` MEANS
    `New home from a building contractor` WITH
        `it replaces a conveyance first executed before 1 July 2022, or rests on an option granted before then` IS TRUE
        `the conveyees agree to acquire title to and the whole beneficial interest in land owned by a building contractor` IS TRUE
        `the building contractor agrees to convey the land to the conveyees`                                IS TRUE
        `the building contractor agrees to build, place, complete or convey a detached, new home on the land` IS TRUE
        `the building contractor owns the land before execution, or will before settlement`               IS TRUE
        `the building contractor bought the land from the person who developed it as a residential lot`  IS TRUE
        `the building contractor paid duty on the land's dutiable value when buying it from the developer` IS TRUE

-- Vacant land for a senior, no home at the relevant time, with only the senior conveyee moving in (s 89A(11AA)).
`a senior's vacant land at $400 000 in 2020` MEANS
    `Home conveyance` WITH
        `the date first executed`                                                         IS YMD 2020 3 1
        `the consideration`                                                               IS 400000
        `the unencumbered value`                                                          IS 400000
        `there is a home on the land at the relevant time`                                IS FALSE
        `it is an off-the-plan contract`                                                  IS FALSE
        `every conveyee is an individual`                                                 IS TRUE
        `at least one conveyee is 18 or older, or is exempted from the age requirement`   IS TRUE
        `at least one conveyee is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`            IS TRUE
        `at least one conveyee is 60 or older at the relevant time`                       IS TRUE
        `at least one conveyee holds an NT pensioner, carer or concession scheme card`     IS FALSE
        `a conveyee or spouse has received the first home owner concession before`        IS FALSE
        `a conveyee or spouse has had a relevant interest in a residence they occupied`   IS TRUE
        `a conveyee or spouse has received a grant, discount, concession or rebate before, not repaid` IS FALSE
        `a conveyee or spouse has had a relevant interest in residential property`        IS TRUE
        `a conveyee or spouse had a relevant interest in Territory residential property in the 24 months before` IS TRUE
        `the Commissioner exempts that Territory interest for a relationship breakdown`   IS FALSE
        `a conveyee already has a beneficial interest in the land`                        IS FALSE
        `the conveyees will acquire the whole beneficial interest in the land`            IS TRUE
        `a conveyee will acquire an interest in the land as trustee`                      IS FALSE
        `every conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence`       IS FALSE
        `at least one conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence` IS TRUE
        `a conveyee who is 60 or older or holds a card will occupy the home`              IS TRUE
        `the Commissioner exempts the conveyees from the occupancy requirement`           IS FALSE
        `the home has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`       IS TRUE
        `the home is substantially renovated new residential premises not occupied or sold since` IS FALSE
        `the Commissioner declares the home a qualifying home`                            IS FALSE
        `a conveyee has been paid, is entitled to or will become entitled to a first home owner grant` IS FALSE
        `the conveyee is paid the grant for a transaction that commenced from 1 January 2015 to 6 May 2019` IS FALSE
        `the conveyees become entitled to possession within 12 months after settlement`   IS TRUE

§§ `ss 4AB and Schedule 1 cl 1(2) -- dutiable value and the scale`

-- s 4AB(1)(a): the greater of the consideration and the unencumbered value; (b): no consideration, the value.
#ASSERT `the dutiable value` 600000 620000 EQUALS 620000
#ASSERT `the dutiable value` 650000 600000 EQUALS 650000
#ASSERT `the dutiable value` 0 500000 EQUALS 500000

-- cl 1(2)(a), V = 300: 0.06571441 x 90 000 + 4 500 = 10 414.2969.
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 300000 EQUALS 10414.2969
-- V = 412.345: 0.06571441 x 170 028.399025 + 6 185.175 = 17 358.49092517245025.
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 412345 EQUALS 17358.49092517245025
-- V = 525: 0.06571441 x 275 625 + 7 875 = 25 987.53425625 (finding 1).
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 525000 EQUALS 25987.53425625
-- Finding 1: the formula and the 4.95% rate meet at $525 000, 3.425625 cents apart -- so "V2" is V squared.
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 525000 MINUS (525000 TIMES 4.95 DIVIDED BY 100) EQUALS 0.03425625
-- Read as V x 2 instead, the formula would give under $8 000 at $525 000 against $25 987.50 above it.
#ASSERT (0.06571441 TIMES 525 TIMES 2) PLUS (15 TIMES 525) LESS THAN 8000
-- cl 1(2)(b)-(d), on the whole value.
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 525001 EQUALS 25987.5495
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 600000 EQUALS 29700
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 2999999 EQUALS 148499.9505
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 3000000 EQUALS 172500
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 4999999 EQUALS 287499.9425
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 5000000 EQUALS 297500
-- The cliffs (finding 5): cl 1(2)(c) and (d) apply at "$3 000 000 or more" and "$5 000 000 or more", so the jump comes
-- on reaching each threshold. Going from $2 999 999 to $3 000 000 adds $24 000.0495; from $4 999 999 to $5 000 000,
-- $10 000.0575. One dollar over $3 000 000 adds only 5.75 cents.
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 3000000 MINUS `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 2999999 EQUALS 24000.0495
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 5000000 MINUS `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 4999999 EQUALS 10000.0575
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 3000001 MINUS `the Schedule 1 cl 1(2) duty on` 3000000 EQUALS 0.0575
-- cl 1(3): two joint tenants of a home worth $800 000 convey it to one of them: a half share, $400 000, plus $5.
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 cl 1(3) duty on a joint tenancy conveyance` 400000 EQUALS 16519.3056
-- Finding 21: the duty payable is rounded down to 5 cents (TAA s 27): $16 519.3056 is payable as $16 519.30. A half share
-- of $824 690 ($412 345): $17 358.49092517245025 + $5 = $17 363.49092517245025, payable as $17 363.45.
#ASSERT `the duty payable on a joint tenancy conveyance first executed on` (YMD 2026 3 1) 400000 EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 16519.3
#ASSERT `the duty payable on a joint tenancy conveyance first executed on` (YMD 2026 3 1) 412345 EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 17363.45
#ASSERT `the duty payable on a joint tenancy conveyance first executed on` (YMD 2017 6 30) 400000 EQUALS `not covered` `the conveyance or registration is dated before 1 July 2017, when Schedule 1 was last amended (No. 13, 2017); the scale in force before then is not in the deposited reprint`

-- The deposited Schedule 1 is applied from 1 July 2017 only.
#ASSERT `the deposited Schedule 1 applies on` (YMD 2017 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`the deposited Schedule 1 applies on` (YMD 2017 6 30))
#ASSERT `the Schedule 1 duty on the conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2015 3 1) 500000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not covered` `the conveyance or registration is dated before 1 July 2017, when Schedule 1 was last amended (No. 13, 2017); the scale in force before then is not in the deposited reprint`

§§ `ss 50, 9(7) -- who is liable`

#ASSERT `who is liable for the duty on` `a conveyance` EQUALS `the conveyee (s 50(a))`
#ASSERT `who is liable for the duty on` `a transaction for which the Act makes no particular party liable` EQUALS `every party, jointly and severally (s 9(7))`

§§ `s 9 -- lodge within 60 days, pay by the last day for lodgement`

#ASSERT `the days to pay the duty` 0 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the days to pay the duty` 90 EQUALS 90
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 9 -- lodge within 60 days after first execution, and pay by the last day for lodgement` FALSE TRUE 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the conveyee` `lodge the instrument with the Commissioner for assessment` 45), (EVENT `the conveyee` `pay the duty` 60)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A notice of assessment fixing day 90: payment on day 85 is in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 9 -- lodge within 60 days after first execution, and pay by the last day for lodgement` FALSE TRUE 90) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the conveyee` `lodge the instrument with the Commissioner for assessment` 30), (EVENT `the conveyee` `pay the duty` 85)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- An exempt conveyance (s 90D, s 91, Schedule 2 item 6 or 7) must still be lodged; nothing is paid.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 9 -- lodge within 60 days after first execution, and pay by the last day for lodgement` FALSE FALSE 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the conveyee` `lodge the instrument with the Commissioner for assessment` 50)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 9(3A): a conveyance that does not proceed, with no sub-sale: nothing to lodge or pay.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 9 -- lodge within 60 days after first execution, and pay by the last day for lodgement` TRUE TRUE 0) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the conveyee, "s 9(1)(a), (6)(a): ..." (lodged on day 61)
#TRACE `s 9 -- lodge within 60 days after first execution, and pay by the last day for lodgement` FALSE TRUE 0 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the conveyee` DOES `pay the duty` AT 40
    PARTY `the conveyee` DOES `lodge the instrument with the Commissioner for assessment` AT 61
-- expect: BREACH BY the conveyee, "s 9(5), (6)(b): ..." (lodged on day 20, paid on day 61, no later date fixed)
#TRACE `s 9 -- lodge within 60 days after first execution, and pay by the last day for lodgement` FALSE TRUE 0 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the conveyee` DOES `lodge the instrument with the Commissioner for assessment` AT 20
    PARTY `the conveyee` DOES `pay the duty` AT 61
-- expect: BREACH BY the conveyee, "s 9(1)(a), (3): an exempt conveyance ... must still be lodged ..." (never lodged)
#TRACE `s 9 -- lodge within 60 days after first execution, and pay by the last day for lodgement` FALSE FALSE 0 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 61)

§§ `s 88A and the date windows (finding 2)`

-- The Territory home owner discount: open on 30 June 2021, closed from 1 July 2021.
#ASSERT `the conveyees are entitled to` `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2021 6 30) 500000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyees are entitled to` `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2021 7 1) 500000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- The senior, pensioner and carer concession has no end date of its own; s 88A closes it on the same day.
#ASSERT `the conveyees are entitled to` `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2021 6 30) 600000 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyees are entitled to` `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2021 7 1) 600000 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`READING: s 89AAB(1) is an express provision displacing s 88A`)
-- The other windows: s 89(1A) before 4 December 2012; s 89AA(1) 24 May 2016 to 6 May 2019; s 90(1AA) before 8 February 2019.
#ASSERT `the conveyees are entitled to` `the first home owner concession (s 89)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2011 3 1) 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyees are entitled to` `the first home owner concession (s 89)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2012 12 4) 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the conveyees are entitled to` `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2019 5 6) 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyees are entitled to` `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2019 5 7) 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the conveyees are entitled to` `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2019 2 7) 500000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyees are entitled to` `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2019 2 8) 500000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- Finding 24: s 102(1). From 4 May 2010 the amended text answers; before then the answer is not covered, not a TRUE or
-- FALSE from the amended text. A first home buyer at $400 000 with a home on the land meets every s 89(1) condition.
#ASSERT `the conveyees' entitlement, apart from s 90B, to` `the first home owner concession (s 89)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2010 5 4) 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `yes, apart from s 90B: only the one concession of greatest benefit can be had`
#ASSERT `the conveyees' entitlement, apart from s 90B, to` `the first home owner concession (s 89)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2010 5 3) 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not covered here` `the conveyance was first executed before 4 May 2010; the home concessions as they stood before the 2010 amendments (s 102) are not in the deposited reprint`
#ASSERT `the conveyees' entitlement, apart from s 90B, to` `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2009 3 1) 500000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not covered here` `the conveyance was first executed before 4 May 2010; the home concessions as they stood before the 2010 amendments (s 102) are not in the deposited reprint`
#ASSERT `the conveyees' entitlement, apart from s 90B, to` `the first home owner concession (s 89)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2012 12 4) 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no`

§§ `A 2026 purchase: no Division 2 concession at all`

-- A first home buyer in March 2026 meets every condition, but s 88A closed the Division on 30 June 2021.
#ASSERT `the home concession for the conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2026 3 1) 600000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no Part 5 Division 2 concession: the Division does not apply to a conveyance first executed after 30 June 2021 (s 88A)`
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2026 3 1) 600000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a building contractor who bought the land from someone other than the developer` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 29700
-- $412 345 in 2026: $17 358.49092517245025, rounded down to 5 cents (TAA s 27): $17 358.45.
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2026 3 1) 412345 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a building contractor who bought the land from someone other than the developer` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 17358.45

§§ `ss 89AA, 89AAB, 89A, 90 and 90B -- the concessions in their windows`

-- First home owner discount, 1 November 2018, an established home at $450 000: duty $20 057.168025, all of it.
#ASSERT `the home concession for the conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 450000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the conveyee is entitled to` `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)` 20057.168025
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 450000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
-- At $600 000: discount = duty on $500 000 = $23 928.6025; $29 700 less that is $5 771.3975, rounded $5 771.35.
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 600000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 5771.35
-- At $700 000, above the $650 000 threshold amount, the definition gives no discount: full duty $34 650.
#ASSERT `the home concession for the conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 700000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no Part 5 Division 2 concession: the conditions of none of them are met`
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 700000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 34650
-- The first home owner discount is for an established home: a new home does not qualify.
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyees are entitled to` `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 450000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- Nor with a first home owner grant (s 89AA(2)(k)).
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyees are entitled to` `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 450000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))

-- Territory home owner discount, 1 March 2020, $500 000, a buyer from interstate with no Territory property:
-- $23 928.6025 less $18 601 = $5 327.6025, rounded $5 327.60. Not limited to first home buyers.
#ASSERT `the home concession for the conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2020 3 1) 500000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the conveyee is entitled to` `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` 18601
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2020 3 1) 500000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 5327.6
-- At the $650 000 threshold: $32 175 less $18 601 = $13 574. One dollar over: no discount, $32 175.0495 rounded $32 175.
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2020 3 1) 650000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 13574
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2020 3 1) 650001 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 32175
-- The same purchase on 1 July 2021: s 88A; full duty, $23 928.6025 rounded $23 928.60.
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2021 7 1) 500000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 23928.6
-- Territory property in the 24 months before: no Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB(2)(d)) ...
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyees are entitled to` `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2020 3 1) 500000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- ... and none with a first home owner grant: the s 90AB reading (finding 11). s 89AAC is not engaged here, as its
-- subsection (1)(a) reaches only grants for transactions that commenced before 7 May 2019.
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyees are entitled to` `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2020 3 1) 500000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE))

-- Senior, pensioner and carer concession, 1 March 2020, a senior who sold a Territory home, $700 000 with a home:
-- $34 650 less $10 000 = $24 650.
#ASSERT `the home concession for the conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2020 3 1) 700000 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the conveyee is entitled to` `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` 10000
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2020 3 1) 700000 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 24650
-- s 90B: a senior from interstate, $600 000: the Territory home owner discount ($18 601) beats the senior concession
-- ($10 000): $29 700 less $18 601 = $11 099.
#ASSERT `the greatest amount in` (`the concessions the conveyees would be entitled to apart from s 90B` (`a purchase` (YMD 2020 3 1) 600000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) 29700) EQUALS 18601
#ASSERT `the home concession for the conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2020 3 1) 600000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the conveyee is entitled to` `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` 18601
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2020 3 1) 600000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 11099
-- With a first home owner grant, no senior concession (s 89A(1)(ga)).
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyees are entitled to` `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2020 3 1) 700000 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
-- s 89A(1)(h): vacant land is capped at $385 000; at $400 000 no concession. s 89A(11AA): one senior moving in is enough.
#ASSERT NOT (`the dutiable value is within the $750 000 or $385 000 cap` `a senior's vacant land at $400 000 in 2020`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyees are entitled to` `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` `a senior's vacant land at $400 000 in 2020`)

-- s 90B(3)(b): 1 March 2019, a first home buyer of an established home at $400 000 is entitled to both discounts, each
-- equal to the whole duty of $16 514.3056; the Commissioner chooses; nil to pay.
#ASSERT `the home concession for the conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2019 3 1) 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `concessions of equal benefit: the Commissioner determines which (s 90B(3)(b))` 16514.3056
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2019 3 1) 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
-- At $600 000 on the same day: discount $23 928.6025 beats $18 601.
#ASSERT `the home concession for the conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2019 3 1) 600000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the conveyee is entitled to` `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)` 23928.6025

-- Principal place of residence rebate, 1 November 2018, a new home at $500 000, not a first home: $7 000 off
-- $23 928.6025 = $16 928.6025, rounded $16 928.60. With a first home owner grant: none (s 90(1)(fa)).
#ASSERT `the home concession for the conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 500000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the conveyee is entitled to` `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)` 7000
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 500000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 16928.6
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 500000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 23928.6
-- The rebate is for a qualifying home (s 90AA): an established home does not qualify.
#ASSERT `the home is a qualifying home for s 90` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 500000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the home is an established home` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 500000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyees are entitled to` `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2018 11 1) 500000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

-- The first home owner concession of 2011 is within its window, but its amount needs the Schedule 1 of 2011.
#ASSERT `the home concession for the conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2011 3 1) 400000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the concession is not covered` `the conveyance or registration is dated before 1 July 2017, when Schedule 1 was last amended (No. 13, 2017); the scale in force before then is not in the deposited reprint`

-- The s 88(1) amounts, given the duty assessed.
-- First home owner discount (a), 1 July 2016: 50% of $10 414.2969 = $5 207.14845, under $10 000.
#ASSERT `the amount of` `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2016 7 1) 300000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) 10414.2969 EQUALS 5207.14845
-- (c), 1 October 2016, above the threshold: $10 000.
#ASSERT `the amount of` `the first home owner discount (s 89AA)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2016 10 1) 700000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) 34650 EQUALS 10000
-- First home owner concession: the lesser of the duty and the duty on $540 000 ($26 730).
#ASSERT `the amount of` `the first home owner concession (s 89)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2011 3 1) 600000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) 29700 EQUALS 26730
-- Senior concession before 28 April 2015: $8 500; principal place of residence rebate before 4 December 2012: $3 500.
#ASSERT `the amount of` `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2015 4 27) 600000 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) 29700 EQUALS 8500
#ASSERT `the amount of` `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2012 12 3) 600000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) 29700 EQUALS 3500
#ASSERT `the amount of` `the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)` (`a purchase` (YMD 2012 12 4) 600000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) 2000 EQUALS 2000

§§ `The period for occupancy and the prescribed period`

#ASSERT `the period for occupancy, in months after possession` `a home is built on the land` 0 0 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the period for occupancy, in months after possession` `no home yet: the conveyees are owner builders or have a comprehensive home building contract` 30 0 EQUALS 42
#ASSERT `the period for occupancy, in months after possession` `no home yet: the conveyees are owner builders or have a comprehensive home building contract` 54 0 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the period for occupancy, in months after possession` `no home yet: the conveyees have an off-the-plan contract` 0 0 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the period for occupancy, in months after possession` `a home is built on the land` 0 24 EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `the prescribed period, in months` EQUALS 6

§§ `The notice of failure to occupy, and the reassessment`

`one of two buyers moves out` MEANS
    `Occupancy failure` WITH
        `this conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                         IS TRUE
        `every conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                        IS FALSE
        `another conveyee has already given the notice`                      IS FALSE
        `this conveyee has an exemption from the occupancy requirement`      IS FALSE
        `the failure has occurred`                                           IS TRUE
        `the Commissioner is of the opinion there are special reasons not to reassess` IS FALSE

`the buyers never move in` MEANS
    `Occupancy failure` WITH
        `this conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                         IS TRUE
        `every conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                        IS TRUE
        `another conveyee has already given the notice`                      IS FALSE
        `this conveyee has an exemption from the occupancy requirement`      IS FALSE
        `the failure has occurred`                                           IS TRUE
        `the Commissioner is of the opinion there are special reasons not to reassess` IS FALSE

`the buyers never move in, and the other buyer has told the Commissioner` MEANS
    `Occupancy failure` WITH
        `this conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                         IS TRUE
        `every conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                        IS TRUE
        `another conveyee has already given the notice`                      IS TRUE
        `this conveyee has an exemption from the occupancy requirement`      IS FALSE
        `the failure has occurred`                                           IS TRUE
        `the Commissioner is of the opinion there are special reasons not to reassess` IS FALSE

`the buyers never move in, with special reasons` MEANS
    `Occupancy failure` WITH
        `this conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                         IS TRUE
        `every conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                        IS TRUE
        `another conveyee has already given the notice`                      IS FALSE
        `this conveyee has an exemption from the occupancy requirement`      IS FALSE
        `the failure has occurred`                                           IS TRUE
        `the Commissioner is of the opinion there are special reasons not to reassess` IS TRUE

-- ss 89AAB(16)(d) and 90D(6)(a): one of two buyers moving out needs no notice; s 89A(3) puts it on that buyer.
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyee must give notice of the failure to occupy` `s 89AAB(7) -- Territory home owner discount` `one of two buyers moves out`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyee must give notice of the failure to occupy` `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor` `one of two buyers moves out`)
#ASSERT `the conveyee must give notice of the failure to occupy` `s 89A(3) -- senior, pensioner and carer concession` `one of two buyers moves out`
#ASSERT `the conveyee must give notice of the failure to occupy` `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor` `the buyers never move in`
-- ss 89AAB(16)(e), 90D(6)(b): only one conveyee need give it.
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyee must give notice of the failure to occupy` `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor` `the buyers never move in, and the other buyer has told the Commissioner`)
-- The Commissioner must reassess (s 90D(8)) unless there are special reasons; s 89AA has no such duty.
#ASSERT `the Commissioner must reassess after the failure to occupy` `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor` `the buyers never move in`
#ASSERT NOT (`the Commissioner must reassess after the failure to occupy` `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor` `the buyers never move in, with special reasons`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Commissioner must reassess after the failure to occupy` `s 89AA(6) -- first home owner discount` `the buyers never move in`)
#ASSERT `the days to notify a failure to occupy` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty for not notifying, in penalty units` EQUALS 50
-- Notice on day 20, reassessment on day 50: both duties done.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the notice of failure to occupy, and the reassessment that follows` `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor` `the buyers never move in`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the conveyee` `give the Commissioner written notice of the failure to occupy` 20), (EVENT `the Commissioner` `reassess duty on the conveyance without the concession` 50)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 89AA: notice on day 30 is all there is.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the notice of failure to occupy, and the reassessment that follows` `s 89AA(6) -- first home owner discount` `the buyers never move in`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the conveyee` `give the Commissioner written notice of the failure to occupy` 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the conveyee, "ss 89(3), ... 90D(5): written notice ... within 30 days ...; maximum penalty 50 penalty units"
#TRACE `the notice of failure to occupy, and the reassessment that follows` `s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor` `the buyers never move in` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)
-- expect: the Commissioner's reassessment still pending (no period is stated for it)
#TRACE `the notice of failure to occupy, and the reassessment that follows` `s 89AAB(7) -- Territory home owner discount` `the buyers never move in` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the conveyee` DOES `give the Commissioner written notice of the failure to occupy` AT 10

§§ `ss 90A and 90AB -- the grant and the concessions`

#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 90A(2), 90AB(2) -- a grant paid after the concession means a reassessment without it` `the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A)` TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Commissioner` `reassess duty on the conveyance without the concession` 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 90A(2), 90AB(2) -- a grant paid after the concession means a reassessment without it` `the first home owner concession (s 89)` TRUE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 90A(4) -- no grant after all means a reassessment with the concession` TRUE TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Commissioner` `reassess duty on the conveyance with the concession` 40)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 90A(4) -- no grant after all means a reassessment with the concession` TRUE TRUE FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 40)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the Commissioner's reassessment without the Territory home owner discount, pending
#TRACE `ss 90A(2), 90AB(2) -- a grant paid after the concession means a reassessment without it` `the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB)` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
-- TAA s 21(4)(c): s 90A(5) lifts the 5-year limit; s 90AB and s 89AA do not.
#ASSERT `the Stamp Duty Act authorises the reassessment after 5 years` `the first home owner grant, after the senior, pensioner and carer concession or the rebate (s 90A)`
#ASSERT NOT (`the Stamp Duty Act authorises the reassessment after 5 years` `the first home owner grant, after the Territory home owner discount (s 90AB)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Stamp Duty Act authorises the reassessment after 5 years` `a failure to occupy after the first home owner discount (s 89AA)`)
#ASSERT `the Stamp Duty Act authorises the reassessment after 5 years` `a failure to occupy the home (ss 89(4), 89AAB(4), 89A(6), 90(4), 90D(8))`

§§ `Part 5 Division 2A -- a new home from a building contractor (s 90D)`

-- 1 March 2026, $650 000, every condition met: exempt, nothing to pay.
#ASSERT `the conveyance is exempt under s 90D` (`a purchase` (YMD 2026 3 1) 650000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `a building contractor who meets s 90D`
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2026 3 1) 650000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `a building contractor who meets s 90D` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
-- No cap on value and no first-home condition: a repeat buyer at $2 000 000 is exempt (otherwise $99 000).
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2026 3 1) 2000000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `a building contractor who meets s 90D` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2026 3 1) 2000000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `a building contractor who bought the land from someone other than the developer` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 99000
-- The window: 1 July 2022 to 30 June 2027.
#ASSERT `the conveyance is exempt under s 90D` (`a purchase` (YMD 2027 6 30) 650000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `a building contractor who meets s 90D`
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance is exempt under s 90D` (`a purchase` (YMD 2027 7 1) 650000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `a building contractor who meets s 90D`)
#ASSERT `the duty payable on the home conveyance` (`a purchase` (YMD 2027 7 1) 650000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `a building contractor who meets s 90D` EQUALS `the duty, in dollars, is` 32175
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance is exempt under s 90D` (`a purchase` (YMD 2022 6 30) 650000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `a building contractor who meets s 90D`)
-- s 90D(1)(a): a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022 is outside it.
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance is exempt under s 90D` (`a purchase` (YMD 2026 3 1) 650000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `a replacement of a contract signed before 1 July 2022`)
-- s 90D(2)(g): the builder must have bought the lot from its developer.
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance is exempt under s 90D` (`a purchase` (YMD 2026 3 1) 650000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `a building contractor who bought the land from someone other than the developer`)

§§ `Part 5 Division 3 -- relationship breakdown (s 91)`

GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `Settlement instrument`
      `the order or agreement date` IS A DATE
      `after the breakdown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Relationship settlement`
`a settlement` MEANS
    `Relationship settlement` WITH
        `the parties are or were married or in a de facto relationship under the Family Law Act` IS TRUE
        `the date of the conveyance`                                                            IS YMD 2026 3 1
        `the instrument`                                                                        IS `the instrument`
        `the date the order was made or the agreement was made`                                 IS `the order or agreement date`
        `the conveyance occurred after the relationship irretrievably broke down`              IS `after the breakdown`
        `the terms of the conveyance are consistent with the order or agreement`                IS TRUE

-- Conveyance 1 March 2026; Family Court order 15 February 2027 (within 12 months): exempt. 1 March 2027 is still within
-- 12 months (READING: "within 12 months after" includes the anniversary); 2 March 2027 is not.
#ASSERT `the conveyance is exempt under s 91` (`a settlement` `a Family Court order under Part VIII or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act` (YMD 2027 2 15) TRUE)
#ASSERT `the conveyance is exempt under s 91` (`a settlement` `a Family Court order under Part VIII or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act` (YMD 2027 3 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance is exempt under s 91` (`a settlement` `a Family Court order under Part VIII or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act` (YMD 2027 3 2) TRUE))
-- s 91(2): a binding financial agreement counts only for a conveyance after the irretrievable breakdown.
#ASSERT `the conveyance is exempt under s 91` (`a settlement` `a binding financial agreement under Part VIIIA or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act` (YMD 2026 9 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance is exempt under s 91` (`a settlement` `a binding financial agreement under Part VIIIA or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act` (YMD 2026 9 1) FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the conveyance is exempt under s 91` (`a settlement` `no order or agreement yet` (YMD 2026 9 1) TRUE))
-- s 91(3): duty paid before the order must be refunded.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 91(3) -- the Commissioner must refund duty paid before the conveyance became exempt` (`a settlement` `a Family Court order under Part VIII or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act` (YMD 2027 2 15) TRUE) TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Commissioner` `refund the duty paid` 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the Commissioner's refund still pending
#TRACE `s 91(3) -- the Commissioner must refund duty paid before the conveyance became exempt` (`a settlement` `a Family Court order under Part VIII or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act` (YMD 2027 2 15) TRUE) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 90)

